# Resolved by `op run` whenever the engine runs: the publisher, the link
# push, the server with its worker. Committed on purpose: every op:// below
# is a REFERENCE, not a value.
#
#   op run --env-file=engine/engine.env -- ./engine/engine.py <command>
#
# op run refuses to start when a reference does not resolve, so only items
# that exist are named here; each platform adapter joins this file with its
# credentials when it is written. Browsing the screens needs none of them:
# `./engine/engine.py serve` runs bare and the worker simply skips what it
# cannot publish, saying so.
# The key that signs a guest's session cookie and binds a sign-in code to
# the browser that asked for it (engine/guests.py). Persistent so a restart
# keeps every guest signed in; without it the engine makes one up for the
# process and says so.
ENGINE_SESSION_KEY=op://Engineering/Engine session key/credential
# Mail from the engine (engine/mail.py): the office account on Stalwart,
# submitted over 465. Host, port and addresses are in config.json.
MAIL_USER=op://Engineering/Stalwart podcast submission/username
MAIL_PASSWORD=op://Engineering/Stalwart podcast submission/credential
# Linear (engine/linear.py): the OAuth application "AgentSee Engine" and the
# refresh token its consent minted (tools/linear.py auth). The token is read
# from the vault live at refresh time, not from this copy: Linear rotates it
# on every use and the engine writes the replacement back (config.json,
# "linear").
LINEAR_CLIENT_ID=op://Engineering/Linear podcast app/username
LINEAR_CLIENT_SECRET=op://Engineering/Linear podcast app/credential
LINEAR_REFRESH_TOKEN=op://Engineering/Linear podcast token/credential
# The office's assistant (engine/idea.py): the service account key from the
# Console workspace "Podcast engine", under its monthly cap (AGE-115, step
# 4). The model and the caps per guest are in config.json, "idea".
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=op://Engineering/Anthropic podcast key/credential
YOUTUBE_CLIENT_ID=op://Engineering/YouTube podcast client/username
YOUTUBE_CLIENT_SECRET=op://Engineering/YouTube podcast client/credential
YOUTUBE_REFRESH_TOKEN=op://Engineering/YouTube podcast token/credential
# The podcast token (opentofu-podcast): KV for the short links, and, for the
# collector, the two Analytics Engine datasets through the SQL endpoint,
# which needs Account > Account Analytics > Read on it.
CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=op://Engineering/Cloudflare podcast token/credential
# The archive bucket (engine/archive.py): the release records and the files
# when they are not on this machine, and the nightly copy of the ledger.
# R2's S3 token scoped to the two podcast buckets, the item tools/stage.env
# resolves; the two plain values are identifiers, not secrets.
R2_ACCOUNT_ID=9468eccb7caed9f96283a9139c37a4df
R2_ARCHIVE_BUCKET=agentsee-podcast-archive
AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=op://Engineering/R2 podcast token/username
AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=op://Engineering/R2 podcast token/credential
# Bluesky (engine/publish/bluesky.py): the handle, and an app password made
# at Settings > Privacy and security > App passwords. An API Credential
# item, like the others, so the field is `credential`.
BLUESKY_IDENTIFIER=op://Engineering/Bluesky podcast token/username
BLUESKY_APP_PASSWORD=op://Engineering/Bluesky podcast token/credential
# Mastodon (engine/publish/mastodon.py): the access token of an application
# the account made at Preferences > Development (write:media,
# write:statuses). The instance is the one in the handle in accounts.json.
MASTODON_ACCESS_TOKEN=op://Engineering/Mastodon podcast token/credential
# X (engine/publish/x.py): the app, and the account's OAuth 2.0 refresh
# token, the same four references as tools/x.env. The token is read from
# the vault live at refresh time, not from this copy: X retires it on every
# use and the adapter writes the replacement back (config.json, "x").
X_APP_ID=op://Engineering/X podcast app/username
X_APP_SECRET=op://Engineering/X podcast app/credential
X_TOKEN=op://Engineering/X podcast token/username
X_TOKEN_SECRET=op://Engineering/X podcast token/credential
